[Event "Knight School"]
[Opening "Caro-Kann Defence"]
[Variation "Advance Variation, Van der Wiel Attack"]
[ECO "B12"]
[Character "solid,positional"]
[Risk "medium"]
[EarlyMate "none"]
[Tricks "none"]
[Themes "c5-break,bishop-retreat"]
[For "black"]
[Kind "sideline"]
[Opponent "4.Nc3"]
[Start "short-system 3...Bf5"]

4. Nc3 e6 { Supports d5 and keeps everything protected. If White now plays 5.Nf3, the game is the Short line by a different move order. } 5. g4 { Chases the bishop, but it also loosens White's own kingside. } ( 5. Nf3 { The most common move. It is the same position as 4.Nf3 e6 5.Nc3: Black plays ...c5. } ) ( 5. a3 c5 ) ( 5. h3 c5 ) ( 5. Bf4 c5 { Hits d4 at once: the bishop on f4 guards e5 but not d4. } ) ( 5. Bd3 Bxd3 6. Qxd3 { The same position as 4.Bd3 Bxd3 5.Qxd3 e6 6.Nc3: Black plays ...c5. } ) 5... Bg6 { The bishop keeps its diagonal and stays outside the pawn chain. Do not take material on c2 or e4: the bishop is worth more than the pawn. } 6. Nge2 ( 6. h4 h5 7. Bg5 Be7 8. Bxe7 Qxe7 ) 6... c5 { Hits d4 straight away, before White can build up with h4 and Bg5. } 7. h4 h6 { Stops h5, which would trap the bishop on g6 and win it. } 8. Be3 Ne7 { The knight heads for c6, where it attacks d4, and leaves d7 free for the other knight. White's kingside pawns have moved far from home, so Black can play against d4 and keep the bishop safe. If White leaves the book, keep hitting d4 and keep ...h6. } *
